    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15107" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eclīgma</span></b> , ătis,
			n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκλειγμα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a medicine to be taken
				by letting it melt in the mouth</i>, <i>an
				electuary</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 21, 21, 89, § 154</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">24, 7, 23, §
				38</span></i>; <i><span class="en">26, 8, 35,
				§ 110</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ecligmătĭum</span></b> ,
			ii, <i>dim. n.</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Theod. Prisc. 2, 17</span></i>.</div>
